WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:02.799
Hi, I'm Fresnel!

00:00:02.799 --> 00:00:06.792
Here is how PanSt3R segments a whole scene from loose photos,

00:00:06.792 --> 00:00:08.244
in one forward pass.

00:00:09.558 --> 00:00:12.762
One shared set of queries looks at every view at once, so

00:00:12.762 --> 00:00:14.898
each object gets one id across the scene.

00:00:18.608 --> 00:00:20.736
The usual way segments each image alone.

00:00:20.736 --> 00:00:24.080
The ids disagree, so a NeRF or splat is fitted for

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:25.295
hours to fix them.

00:00:25.715 --> 00:00:27.741
PanSt3R reads every view together.

00:00:27.741 --> 00:00:30.983
One id per object, and no camera poses.

00:00:32.758 --> 00:00:35.674
Loose photos go into two frozen networks.

00:00:35.674 --> 00:00:40.256
MUSt3R gives geometry that knows which patches are the same surface.

00:00:40.256 --> 00:00:41.505
DINOv2 gives semantics.

00:00:41.925 --> 00:00:46.590
Their features become frame tokens, and every view's tokens join one long sequence.

00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:50.019
Two hundred learned queries cross-attend to that whole sequence.

00:00:50.019 --> 00:00:52.360
Each query sees every view at once.

00:00:52.780 --> 00:00:56.611
Each refined query becomes a mask in every view, and one class.

00:00:56.611 --> 00:00:57.888
Same query, same id.

00:00:57.888 --> 00:00:58.845
Nothing to match.

00:01:00.608 --> 00:01:04.473
The raw masks overlap, so the paper picks a subset with one

00:01:04.473 --> 00:01:06.083
binary optimisation over the scene.

00:01:06.503 --> 00:01:09.738
Every chosen mask earns its area, summed over all views.

00:01:10.158 --> 00:01:13.379
Every overlapping pair costs its overlap, times a penalty.

00:01:15.258 --> 00:01:18.943
With the standard merge, a duplicate can outbid the real object, and

00:01:18.943 --> 00:01:20.172
black void blocks appear.

00:01:20.592 --> 00:01:23.808
With QUBO choosing over the whole scene, most holes fill in.

00:01:25.508 --> 00:01:30.049
On ScanNet the paper reports sixty five point seven, ahead of the lifting methods.

00:01:30.049 --> 00:01:34.265
But rendering the test views needs a splat that takes thirty five minutes.

00:01:35.558 --> 00:01:37.402
Move the reconciliation into attention.

00:01:37.402 --> 00:01:41.460
Queries that see every view give ids that agree by construction.

00:01:43.108 --> 00:01:47.270
Frozen features from all views, shared queries, and a merge for the whole scene.

00:01:47.708 --> 00:01:49.862
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:49.862 --> 00:01:50.478
I'm Fresnel.

00:01:50.478 --> 00:01:50.786
Bye!
